-- title:
--   Left Right Tensor Prefix Point Measurement Adjoint Normalization
-- statement:
--   **Adjoint point-measurement prefixes are normalized on the left.** With finite submeasurements `A` and `B` and a finite projective measurement `R`, use the same family `D_a` as in the corresponding right-normalization lemma. The adjoint-side sum is also bounded by the identity.
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{a : α} D_a^{\dagger} D_a \le I_{ι \times ι}.
--   $$
--
--   The estimate supplies the adjoint normalization hypothesis for the first reverse step in the evaluated-slice scalar chain, specifically the bound used by `evaluatedSlice_phaseSix_first_reverse_bound`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.leftRightTensor_prefix_pointMeasurement_adjoint_normalization`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
